SEG_0002>if<MATHSEG_0003>\nwith obvious restriction mappings.\n<STRUCT_0003> Let <MATH_0009> be an abelian sheaf on <MATH_0010>. We define\nthe <TEXTITOPEN_0002>extension <MATH_0011> of <MATH_0012> by <MATH_0013><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nto be the sheafification of the abelian presheaf <MATH_0014>.\n<STRUCT_0004> Let <MATH_0015> be a category having an initial object <MATH_0016>.\nLet <MATH_0017> be a presheaf on <MATH_0018> with values in <MATH_0019>.\nWe define the <TEXTITOPEN_0003>extension <MATH_0020> of <MATH_0021> by <MATH_0022><TEXTITCLOSE_0003>\nto be the presheaf on <MATH_0023> with values in <MATH_0024> defined by the\nrule\n<MATHSEG_0004>if<MATHSEG_0005>if<MATHSEG_0006>\nwith obvious restriction mappings.\n<STRUCT_0005> Let <MATH_0025> be a type of algebraic structure\nsuch that <MATH_0026> has an initial object <MATH_0027>.\nLet <MATH_0028> be a sheaf of algebraic structures on <MATH_0029>\n(of the give type). We define the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0004>extension <MATH_0030> of <MATH_0031> by <MATH_0032><TEXTITCLOSE_0004>\nto be the sheafification of the presheaf <MATH_0033>\ndefined above.\n<STRUCT_0006> Let <MATH_0034> be a presheaf of rings on <MATH_0035>.\nLet <MATH_0036> be a presheaf of <MATH_0037>-modules.\nIn this case we define the <TEXTITOPEN_0005>extension by <MATH_0038><TEXTITCLOSE_0005>\nto be the presheaf of <MATH_0039>-modules which is equal to\n<MATH_0040> as an abelian presheaf endowed with\nthe multiplication map\n<MATH_0041>.\n<STRUCT_0007> Let <MATH_0042> be a sheaf of rings on <MATH_0043>.\nLet <MATH_0044> be a sheaf of <MATH_0045>-modules.\nIn this case we define the <TEXTITOPEN_0006>extension by <MATH_0046><TEXTITCLOSE_0006>\nto be the <MATH_0047>-module which is equal to\n<MATH_0048> as an abelian sheaf endowed with\nthe multiplication map <MATH_0049>.\n<STRUCT_0008>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b0f72b1a82822d98c88cd0d69f270adb4948303432e48be1cb4b23db8bbc4008", "unit_id": "tag:00A4:statement"}
